<h1>MDE-POS Multi-Tenant Payment Methods & Custom Channels Implementation Guide</h1>

<div class="callout">
  <strong>System Version:</strong> MDE-POS v1.0.1+<br>
  <strong>Module:</strong> Multi-Tenant Provisioning, Store Settings & POS Checkout Engine<br>
  <strong>Scope:</strong> Turnkey Super Admin Onboarding, Store Self-Service, POS Dynamic Hotkeys, Daraja Express STK Routing
</div>

<h2>1. Executive Summary & Architecture</h2>
<p>
  MDE-POS provides a hybrid, multi-tiered payment configuration architecture designed specifically for modern East African retail and commercial verticals. Store owners can configure and accept payments through Safaricom M-Pesa Buy Goods Tills, Paybill shortcodes, Bank wire / Pesalink, PDQ card swipe machines, Cash drawers, and customer credit balance accounts.
</p>

<h3>The Hybrid Operating Model</h3>
<ol>
  <li>
    <strong>Super Admin Turnkey Provisioning:</strong> During tenant account creation, the Super Admin wizard features a dedicated <em>"2. Payment Channels"</em> tab where primary Till numbers, Paybill shortcodes, card terminals, and cash drawer labels are initialized. Stores are 100% operationally ready the moment they are provisioned.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>Store Owner Self-Service:</strong> Store owners and managers have full access to <code>/settings</code> &rarr; <em>"Payment Methods & Tills"</em> to enable/disable channels, update Till numbers when SIM cards change, configure bank account details, and register custom payment options.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>Super Admin Live Oversight:</strong> Super Admins can inspect and edit payment configurations for any tenant directly from <code>/super-admin/tenants/{id}</code>.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>Dynamic POS Terminal:</strong> The POS checkout modal dynamically renders only enabled store channels, assigns automated keyboard hotkeys (1..N), displays the active Till/Paybill number directly on the cashier screen, and dispatches Safaricom Daraja STK Push requests.
  </li>
</ol>

<h2>2. JSON Data Model & Persistence</h2>
<p>
  Payment channel definitions are stored in the existing <code>tenants.settings</code> JSON column. This eliminates any database schema migrations while providing full extensibility.
</p>

<pre>
{
  "mpesa_till_number": "523910",
  "payment_methods": [
    {
      "id": "cash",
      "name": "Cash",
      "type": "Cash",
      "enabled": true,
      "details": {
        "drawer_label": "Main Cash Drawer",
        "allow_change": true
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "mpesa-till",
      "name": "M-Pesa Buy Goods",
      "type": "Mobile Money",
      "enabled": true,
      "details": {
        "till_number": "523910",
        "store_name": "Nairobi Fresh Mart",
        "stk_push": true
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "mpesa-paybill",
      "name": "M-Pesa Paybill",
      "type": "Mobile Money",
      "enabled": false,
      "details": {
        "business_number": "247247",
        "account_number": "STORE-001"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "card-pdq",
      "name": "Card (PDQ Terminal)",
      "type": "Card",
      "enabled": true,
      "details": {
        "terminal_id": "POS-98102",
        "bank_name": "Equity Bank"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "bank-transfer",
      "name": "Bank Transfer / Pesalink",
      "type": "Bank",
      "enabled": false,
      "details": {
        "bank_name": "KCB Bank",
        "account_number": "1122334455"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "credit",
      "name": "Customer Credit",
      "type": "Credit",
      "enabled": true,
      "details": {}
    }
  ]
}
</pre>

<h2>3. Super Admin Tenant Creation Wizard</h2>
<p>
  Located in <code>resources/js/pages/super-admin/Tenants.vue</code>, the tenant creation dialog contains 4 tabs:
</p>
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Tab Step</th>
      <th>Key Configuration Fields</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>1. Profile & Admin</strong></td>
      <td>Store Name, Subdomain, Currency (KES/USD/UGX/TZS), Business Type, Initial Admin Account.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>2. Payment Channels</strong></td>
      <td>
        &bull; Cash Drawer (Default on, custom drawer label)<br>
        &bull; M-Pesa Buy Goods Till (Till number, branding name, STK push toggle)<br>
        &bull; M-Pesa Paybill (Business number & Account number)<br>
        &bull; Card PDQ (Terminal ID & Bank name)<br>
        &bull; Bank Transfer / Pesalink (Bank & Account number)<br>
        &bull; Customer Credit Accounts
      </td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>3. Devices & POS</strong></td>
      <td>PC Hardware Lock ID, Auto-print on complete, Offline sync interval.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>4. Network & Domain</strong></td>
      <td>Dedicated custom domain and IP access restrictions.</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h2>4. Tenant Store Self-Service (/settings)</h2>
<p>
  Store owners and managers manage channels in <code>resources/js/pages/settings/SettingsIndex.vue</code>:
</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Instant Toggle:</strong> Switch channels on or off in real-time. Deactivated channels immediately disappear from the checkout modal.</li>
  <li><strong>Edit Channel Dialog:</strong> Click <em>"Edit"</em> to update Till numbers, Paybill codes, or Bank credentials.</li>
  <li><strong>Bespoke Custom Channels:</strong> Register custom tender methods (e.g. "Gift Voucher", "Pesalink Wire", "Cheque").</li>
</ul>

<h2>5. POS Terminal Checkout Experience</h2>
<p>
  Located in <code>resources/js/components/pos/PaymentModal.vue</code>:
</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Dynamic Hotkeys:</strong> Methods are assigned numeric badges (1..N). Pressing keys 1 through N switches methods instantly.</li>
  <li><strong>Live Till / Paybill Guidance Strip:</strong> An emerald banner displays the active Till number (e.g. <code>Buy Goods Till: 523910</code>) so cashiers can read it to walk-in customers.</li>
  <li><strong>Express STK Push:</strong> Enter the customer's phone number and press <code>S</code> or <em>"Send STK Push"</em>. Safaricom prompts the customer for their PIN and automatically confirms the sale.</li>
  <li><strong>Split Payments:</strong> Cashiers can split sales across multiple tender types (e.g., KES 1,000 Cash + KES 1,500 M-Pesa Till).</li>
</ul>

<h2>6. Safaricom Daraja Multi-Tenant Routing</h2>
<p>
  Implemented in <code>app/Http/Controllers/MpesaController.php</code>:
</p>
<p>
  The STK Push engine checks whether the current tenant has configured custom Daraja credentials (<code>mpesa_consumer_key</code>, <code>mpesa_consumer_secret</code>, <code>mpesa_passkey</code>). If present, requests are routed directly to Safaricom using the tenant's shortcode. If not specified, the system transparently falls back to central application credentials in <code>.env</code>.
</p>

<h2>7. Thermal Receipt Layout</h2>
<p>
  Thermal receipts generated by <code>resources/js/components/pos/ReceiptModal.vue</code> include:
</p>
<ul>
  <li>Store details, tax invoice number, and cashier identifier.</li>
  <li>Tender breakdown (e.g. <code>Payment (M-Pesa Buy Goods): KES 2,500.00</code>).</li>
  <li>M-Pesa transaction confirmation code (e.g. <code>M-Pesa Code: QKL83910</code>).</li>
  <li>Card terminal authorization code (e.g. <code>Ref / Auth: POS-98102</code>).</li>
  <li>Code 39 vector barcode for optical return and audit scanning.</li>
</ul>

<div class="callout">
  <strong>Summary:</strong> All tenant payment method workflows are operational, backward compatible, and fully integrated across backend provisioning, self-service settings, checkout POS, and thermal receipt printing.
</div>

